==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|а́ккула|о́кула||dialectal (Northern)}}
* {{alter|ru|а́кула||dialectal (Arkhangelsk)}}

===Etymology===
First attested as {{m|ru|а́ккула|g=f}} in 1847 and earlier in the 18th century, {{m|ru|а́ккуле}} in 1789, {{m|ru|акул|g=m}} in 1755.<ref>{{R:ru:SRJa18|а́ккула <small>и</small> акул|38|1|url=01/sl103806}}</ref><ref>{{R:ru:Anikin|аку́ла|135|1}}</ref><ref>{{R:uk:ESUM|аку́ла|58|1}}</ref> {{inh+|ru|zle-mru|-|sc=Cyrs}}, attested only as a derivative {{m|zle-mru|акулий|sc=Cyrs}} used to describe liver oil of a [[Greenland shark]] in a source going back to late 16th or early 17th century.<ref>{{R:ru:SRJa1117|акулий|27|1}}</ref>

{{bor+|ru|smi|-}} language (compare {{cog|sms|akkli}}, {{cog|sjd|а̄һклэӈӈк}}, {{cog|se|áhkạlakkis|t=Greenland shark}}), further borrowed {{der|ru|non|hákarl}} (compare dialectal {{cog|no|håkall}}).

